A||||8||86SE||Whats the dash light right above the tach?||||5||
Z||000000||86SE||01-25-2000||10:06 PM||||I swore I saw that thing blink once but I dident have time to read what it said,  what is that long rectangular box on the instrument panel above the tach?? Is it supposed to come on, because it hasent come on it a year.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||01-25-2000||10:13 PM||||You must have seen something else blink at you.  That space above the tachometer serves no purpose whatsoever.  There is no light installed in it at all although there are two holes in the back of the cluster housing that are shaped like light socket holes.  The only reason I can figure out for it being there is to visually balance the spot for the odometer that is above the speedometer.  Maybe someone out there can come up with a clever use for that spot.||||reg||7
Z||000002||86SE||01-25-2000||10:20 PM||||I figured it would be a perfect place for an upshift light but since there is nothing there i can stop going crazy!!||||reg||8
Z||000004||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||10:44 PM||||On an 88 GT with an Intercooled, Water Injected Turbo, we used that spot for a digital temp readout telling us the temp of the air before and after the intercooler. Ideally this would allow the driver to get out of the turbo if the temps get too high and start detonation.  Besides whats wrong with the upshift light that is already there? It up high so its just in the lower view of vision for those who do not know their engine by ear yet...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fieroguy1||01-25-2000||11:02 PM||||Originally it was designed as a warning indicator for an over heat situation. When this happened it would light,as this was your only warning besides the gauge that engine damage was emminent. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||01-26-2000||04:30 AM||||Doesn't the FDD-X1 use this hole?||||reg||1
Z||000007||fotofrank||01-26-2000||01:19 PM||||Last time I looked in a fiero repair book the rectangular slot was an up shift indicator.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroc4||01-26-2000||05:38 PM||||I thought this might be an ideal spot for a small digital speedometer, for those times that the analog 85mph (120 for some) unit just didn't swing far enough.  In otherwords a useless gadget, because <I><B>NONE</B></I> of us would ever exceed the posted speed limit.||||reg||1
Z||000009||86SE||01-26-2000||05:41 PM||||I have an auto trans, and dont know where the upshift light is, so i figured right there would be the perfect place for one.||||reg||6
